From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - trim the infinite lines LocOpe_SplitDrafts
 hands to GeomFill_Pipe

LocOpe_SplitDrafts::Perform() cannot complete for any input. Every call that
gets past the planar-face check throws Standard_DomainError("No such curve").

Perform() accepts only a planar face: its file-local NewPlane() helper
intersects the neutral plane with the face's own plane and needs a real line.
Past that it builds the two drafted planes, intersects them with GeomInt_IntSS,
and sweeps the resulting curve along the face normal:

  Handle(Geom_Line) theLinePipe = new Geom_Line(NormalFg);
  ...
  thePipe.Init(theLinePipe, i2s.Line(1));

The intersection of two planes is always a Geom_Line, and Geom_Line is
infinite, as is theLinePipe. GeomFill_Pipe::Init() puts the section through
GeomFill_UniformSection, whose constructor calls
GeomConvert::CurveToBSplineCurve(), and that function raises
Standard_DomainError("No such curve") for an untrimmed line by design: its
header documents "Raises DomainError if the curve C is infinite", and an
infinite curve has no B-spline form. Its Geom_TrimmedCurve branch has handled
Geom_Line since the function was written, so a trimmed line converts.

The defect is therefore in the caller, not in GeomConvert: LocOpe_SplitDrafts
passes curves to an API documented to reject them. The same mistake is made a
second time further down Perform(), where the section is the basis curve of a
wire edge, stripped of its Geom_TrimmedCurve wrapper two lines earlier.

Fix: a file-local TrimInfinite() helper that leaves a finite curve alone and
trims an infinite one, from its own origin, to the diagonal of the shape's
bounding box enlarged by that origin, so the trim covers the shape wherever
the line's origin falls. Applied to the pipe path once and to both sections.
Bnd_Box and BRepBndLib are already reachable from TKFeat, TKTopAlgo being in
its EXTERNLIB.

Measured on a 10x10x10 box, splitting its top face along x = 5 with the
neutral plane x = 5 and a 10 degree draft. Before: all four extraction
directions tried throw "No such curve". After: IsDone() is true, the result
has 7 faces against the box's 6, exactly one of them tilted 10 degrees off
the axes, and the volume is 1022.04, which is 1000 plus the wedge the draft
adds (0.5 * 5 * 5*tan(10 deg) * 10 = 22.04).

NOT UPSTREAM-BOUND, and it cannot become so: OCCT master deleted
LocOpe_SplitDrafts outright on 2026-08-07, in Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1442
("Coding, Modeling Algo - Clean up dead headers", 236 files, 24858 deletions,
by maintainer dpasukhi). The class has no caller anywhere in the OCCT tree,
not even a DRAW command, which is presumably why it was removed and why this
defect survived to 8.0.1 unnoticed. This patch is therefore carried for the
V8_0_1 pin alone, and retires by deletion rather than by an upstream merge:
the first kernel bump past #1442 removes the class, and OCCTSwift's own
Shape.splitDrafts has to go with it.

A GTest was written and proven both ways all the same, and is kept at
Scripts/repro/1393-splitdrafts/upstream/LocOpe_SplitDrafts_Test.cxx: it fails
with the exact throw above against the unpatched translation unit and passes
against the patched one.

SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#1393.
---
 .../TKFeat/LocOpe/LocOpe_SplitDrafts.cxx           | 38 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFeat/LocOpe/LocOpe_SplitDrafts.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFeat/LocOpe/LocOpe_SplitDrafts.cxx
@@ -16,8 +16,10 @@
 
 #include <LocOpe_SplitDrafts.hxx>
 
+#include <Bnd_Box.hxx>
 #include <BRep_Builder.hxx>
 #include <BRep_Tool.hxx>
+#include <BRepBndLib.hxx>
 #include <BRepGProp.hxx>
 #include <BRepTools_Substitution.hxx>
 #include <Extrema_ExtPC.hxx>
@@ -81,6 +83,8 @@ static TopoDS_Edge NewEdge(const TopoDS_Edge&,
 
 static bool Contains(const NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape>&, const TopoDS_Shape&);
 
+static occ::handle<Geom_Curve> TrimInfinite(const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>&, const Bnd_Box&);
+
 //=================================================================================================
 
 void LocOpe_SplitDrafts::Init(const TopoDS_Shape& S)
@@ -168,11 +172,17 @@ void LocOpe_SplitDrafts::Perform(const TopoDS_Face& F,
   NCollection_List<TopoDS_Shape>::Iterator itl;
   BRep_Builder                             B;
 
-  occ::handle<Geom_Surface> NewSg       = new Geom_Plane(NewPlg);
-  occ::handle<Geom_Surface> NewSd       = new Geom_Plane(NewPld);
-  occ::handle<Geom_Line>    theLinePipe = new Geom_Line(NormalFg); // ou NormalFd
+  occ::handle<Geom_Surface> NewSg = new Geom_Plane(NewPlg);
+  occ::handle<Geom_Surface> NewSd = new Geom_Plane(NewPld);
   GeomInt_IntSS             i2s(NewSg, NewSd, Precision::Confusion());
 
+  // GeomFill_Pipe converts its path and its section through GeomConvert::CurveToBSplineCurve,
+  // which rejects an infinite curve. Both are lines here, so trim them to the shape.
+  Bnd_Box aShapeBox;
+  BRepBndLib::Add(myShape, aShapeBox);
+  occ::handle<Geom_Curve> theLinePipe =
+    TrimInfinite(new Geom_Line(NormalFg), aShapeBox); // ou NormalFd
+
   NCollection_Map<TopoDS_Shape, TopTools_ShapeMapHasher> theMap;
   occ::handle<GeomAdaptor_Curve>                         HAC = new GeomAdaptor_Curve;
   occ::handle<GeomAdaptor_Surface>                       HAS = new GeomAdaptor_Surface;
@@ -185,7 +195,7 @@ void LocOpe_SplitDrafts::Perform(const TopoDS_Face& F,
 
     GeomFill_Pipe thePipe;
     thePipe.GenerateParticularCase(true);
-    thePipe.Init(theLinePipe, i2s.Line(1));
+    thePipe.Init(theLinePipe, TrimInfinite(i2s.Line(1), aShapeBox));
     thePipe.Perform(true);
     if (!thePipe.IsDone())
     {
@@ -431,7 +441,7 @@ void LocOpe_SplitDrafts::Perform(const TopoDS_Face& F,
 
         GeomFill_Pipe thePipe;
         thePipe.GenerateParticularCase(true);
-        thePipe.Init(theLinePipe, C);
+        thePipe.Init(theLinePipe, TrimInfinite(C, aShapeBox));
         thePipe.Perform(true);
         if (!thePipe.IsDone())
         {
@@ -1974,3 +1984,21 @@ static TopoDS_Edge NewEdge(const TopoDS_Edge&               edg,
   }
   return NewEdg;
 }
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+static occ::handle<Geom_Curve> TrimInfinite(const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>& theCurve,
+                                            const Bnd_Box&                 theBox)
+{
+  if (!Precision::IsInfinite(theCurve->FirstParameter())
+      && !Precision::IsInfinite(theCurve->LastParameter()))
+  {
+    return theCurve;
+  }
+  // The range is measured from the curve's own origin, so that the trim covers the box
+  // wherever that origin lies.
+  Bnd_Box aBox = theBox;
+  aBox.Add(theCurve->Value(0.));
+  const double anExtent = std::max(sqrt(aBox.SquareExtent()), Precision::Confusion());
+  return new Geom_TrimmedCurve(theCurve, -anExtent, anExtent);
+}
